  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "0c325ebe-a46d-4a38-b83f-5992fe74fcf2",
      "target": "d3e7867f-5467-4091-9b7e-448accd5c0a0",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "Two server lists, compared: today Except yesterday is what appeared (web3), yesterday Except today what went away (cache1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "2a4b7cb4-b525-4712-bf96-6883cfaf4f52",
      "target": "76cebb9f-d005-4186-b9b4-23bb58a7ed68",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "Count By tallies each distinct item, most frequent first; Rows goes straight into Table or CSV Format."
    },
    {
      "id": "4d68470b-316e-4c27-8c03-2445692948ad",
      "target": "f8ceb7db-fbae-48ea-a3a9-2c62cd6a7a42",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "Attributes become @name and repeated elements arrays, so JSON Get reads feed.entry[1].title. JSON To XML turns it back into the same XML."
    },
    {
      "id": "50840c24-4768-4b99-8b7e-7104ab991243",
      "target": "7fc1e8aa-2ce8-4ada-80f7-050005ee4943",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "In real use the HTML comes from HTTP Request. The CSS selector a.dl picks the download links, and Base URL makes them absolute, ready for Download To File."
    },
    {
      "id": "531b49b2-5eaa-41bd-8d13-5af5db6c9924",
      "target": "d38bac49-3279-4942-bea5-ff4fcbfeaadd",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "Template runs per item of both lists (right-click an input: For each item). Its right-click menu, Per item, pairs them as every combination: 2 services x 3 environments = 6 host names."
    },
    {
      "id": "fc8d1808-cee0-4853-b6f6-4b47fe33b58d",
      "target": "b898459a-272e-48ab-ac99-e5c625e0c292",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "JSON Get runs once per line. The middle line is not JSON: with Per item \u003E Skip items that fail ticked, its result is left empty and the node warns, instead of failing and taking the other two with it."
    },
    {
      "id": "a8100362-3ca1-45ff-a6f2-f16d406bfe62",
      "target": "fcff5731-0530-4b92-9d02-641cb5d0eefb",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "text": "The List nodes take a list of anything: numbers, booleans and dates as well as text. Range\u0027s numbers go straight into Reverse."
    }
  ]
}